ative to the Earth and the Sun. As the moon orbits around the Earth, different portions of its surface are illuminated by the Sun, creating the phases.\n3. The moon phases include new moon, waxing crescent, first quarter, waxing gibbous, full moon, waning gibbous, third quarter, and waning crescent.\n4. A lunar eclipse occurs when the Earth is directly between the Sun and the Moon, causing the Earth's shadow to fall on the Moon. This happens only occasionally, not every day.", "new_cot_probs": [1.619272885266046e-16, 7.991885625502348e-11, 1.2937139720438427e-15, 4.0708514618116e-16], "cot_prob": [-120.0], "cot_step_prob": [-120.5]}, "2": {"completion": "B) alter the way the moon's fac", "probs": [2.890965738587744e-19, 1.542770902349111e-13, 1.5298513523266135e-17, 1.1433991462277087e-18], "prediction": 1, "target_cot_step": "The question is about moon phases.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Moon phases\n\nChoices:\n(A): change the moon into cheese\n(B): alter the way the moon's facade looks\n(C): change moon lakes into vapor\n(D): cause lunar eclipse every day\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.", "specificity_preds": [2, 0, 0, 2, 3, 1, 3, 3, 2, 1, 3, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 3], "specificity_probs": [[1.891912806303606e-16, 1.428304119230762e-15, 6.978772594534721e-12, 6.265155003815212e-15], [4.1524561567030105e-10, 3.82428030215598e-12, 1.4208923100611504e-11, 7.074206671842109e-13], [7.504603882768635e-11, 1.991517607562946e-14, 2.638332294877064e-14, 7.661859288399231e-16], [7.204172764526014e-15, 5.610615799538608e-15, 7.673383456419103e-11, 1.0586455621635835e-13], [4.6068610894383494e-14, 1.6922204956748566e-11, 2.3129909446084618e-11, 4.945392984012642e-10], [2.4398987333567462e-14, 6.221127779593161e-11, 2.8525308336116786e-14, 3.515007583637002e-15], [2.1378953024130815e-13, 2.860472275711956e-12, 2.578794111845334e-13, 1.3782526508965276e-10], [1.196661178351835e-13, 1.1241592238250137e-13, 7.803212286397465e-13, 1.48702897218022